{
  "_": [
    "The concept layer: what a word MEANS, and whether the bare word is buyable.",
    "",
    "Two halves, and they are shaped differently on purpose.",
    "",
    "1. `intents` assigns an intent to a concept that ALREADY EXISTS as a generic",
    "   product in generics.json. Those 188 rows already carry a name in all six",
    "   languages, so restating the names here would be two copies of one",
    "   translation and the copies would drift. The importer reads the names from",
    "   generics.json and takes only the intent from here.",
    "",
    "   Only the OVERRIDES are listed. Anything in generics.json that is absent",
    "   below is 'generic', which is the honest default for a seed that was",
    "   deliberately built out of things you can shop for without a brand.",
    "",
    "2. `concepts` are brand-new concepts that have NO PRODUCT AND ARE NOT MEANT",
    "   TO. This is the half the old schema could not express at all.",
    "",
    "WHY THE SECOND HALF EXISTS. Fifty concepts were removed from the seed",
    "because the bare word is not enough to shop from: a list saying 'Shampoo'",
    "makes whoever is holding it guess. That judgement was right and is NOT",
    "reversed here -- none of these becomes a product, and none of them can ever",
    "appear as a row in anybody's shopping list.",
    "",
    "What was lost with them was something else entirely: the only place that",
    "knew `shampoo`, `sampon`, `Shampooing` and `champu` are one idea. Removing",
    "the product removed the multilingual anchor, so those four words became four",
    "unrelated cache misses that would never share an answer. A concept restores",
    "the anchor without restoring the product, which is what the two-table split",
    "in 007 is for.",
    "",
    "THE TEST FOR AN INTENT, applied to the search rather than to the list item:",
    "",
    "  generic   the search is for the thing itself. Nobody typing 'morcovi'",
    "            wants a brand of carrot, and asking an external database for one",
    "            is a request nobody was waiting for.",
    "  branded   the search names a category and the person is choosing a",
    "            product. 'apa', 'deodorant', 'detergent'. A generic row here is",
    "            a placeholder that answers nothing, so it must never suppress",
    "            discovery and never outrank a real product.",
    "  mixed     both readings are ordinary. 'lapte' might mean any milk or it",
    "            might mean Zuzu 1.5%. Rank both and prefer neither by rule.",
    "",
    "NOTHING HERE IS A COMMERCIAL FACT. Every string is a common noun translated",
    "into six languages. There are no brands, no sizes, no barcodes and no",
    "ingredients, so there is nothing in this file that could be invented (S4).",
    "",
    "ONE WORD THAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: pepperoni. It is a cured sausage in",
    "English and bell peppers in Italian ('peperoni'), and a concept that",
    "resolves to sausage for an Italian asking about vegetables is worse than no",
    "concept at all. Resolution CAN hold a collision -- see `prune` in",
    "concepts.test.sql -- but only where both readings are worth having. Here one",
    "of them is simply wrong."
  ],

